// Regression fixture for final-review Critical 1 + Critical 2 (memory-
// audit-4e whole-branch review, probe P1): a global `text` pushed into a
// global `list of text`. Before the fix, `cl_free_globals` had no runtime-
// aliasing analysis for globals at all -- it froze `p1Gt`'s handle into
// `p1Gl`'s single element via a plain handle copy, then freed BOTH `p1Gt`
// and (via `p1Gl`'s own element-free loop) the same handle again: SIGSEGV
// at process exit. The 4e/pre-ARC fix disqualified both `p1Gt` (bare-ident
// push-argument handoff) and `p1Gl` (a push whose value fails
// lowEscapeFreshInit disqualifies the receiving container too) from
// `cl_free_globals` -- both leaked instead of double-freeing.
//
// ARC Task 5 (counted container element slots): `p1Gl.push(p1Gt)` now
// retains `p1Gt`'s value BEFORE the push (non-birth: a bare identifier --
// confirmed against the emitted C: `t1 = cv_p1Gt; rt_text_retain(t1);
// rt_list_push(cv_p1Gl, &(t1));`), so `p1Gl` genuinely owns its own +1 of
// the shared text, independent of `p1Gt`'s own reference. Task 5 also
// DELETED the "non-fresh-push disqualifies the receiver" consult
// (lower.cla's old `lowEscapeWalkMethodCall` rule) -- that consult is what
// used to keep `p1Gl` out of `cl_free_globals` entirely; with it gone,
// `p1Gl` now QUALIFIES for a real, DEEP release there (confirmed against
// the emitted C: `cl_free_globals` now contains `{ int32_t i; for (...)
// rt_text_release(*(rt_text **)rt_list_at(cv_p1Gl, i)); }
// rt_list_release(cv_p1Gl);`) -- safe precisely because the element it
// walks is `p1Gl`'s OWN retained copy (rc==2 after the push), so releasing
// it only drops the count back to 1, never to 0.
//
// ARC Task 6 (globals release unconditionally): `cl_free_globals` no longer
// consults `lowGlobalsVarQualifies` at all -- it walks EVERY global,
// including `p1Gt`, which is now released too (declaration order: `p1Gt`
// releases first, dropping the shared text from rc==2 to rc==1; `p1Gl`'s
// deep release then drops its own element copy from 1 to 0, freeing it).
// Expected strict-mode leak count: 0 (../p1_push_global.leaks deleted --
// was 2). Both roots are independently retained (Task 4/5) and both are now
// walked (Task 6), so nothing is left unreleased and nothing double-frees.

var p1Gt: text = "hello"
var p1Gl: list of text

func runP1PushGlobal() {
    p1Gl.push(p1Gt)
    alert("p1 done")
}
